<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Bau</h1><p class="st-meta">1760 CE – 1871 CE (approx.) · capital Bau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Fijian chiefdom ruled from a tiny island off Viti Levu, which became the strongest power in Fiji and under Cakobau led the islands into British rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bau is an islet of a few hectares off the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viti-levu">Viti Levu</a>. In the mid-18th century chiefs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kubuna-confederacy">Kubuna</a> people settled there, and under the war-king title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vunivalu-of-bau">Vunivalu</a> they built a maritime power using the island's fleets of large double canoes and alliances through marriage.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vunivalu-of-bau">Vunivalu</a> shared authority with the senior sacred chief, the Roko Tui Bau, but in practice the war kings came to dominate. In the early 19th century Naulivou used <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">muskets</a> and European beachcombers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-savage">Charles Savage</a> to expand Bau's reach. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanoa-visawaqa">Tanoa Visawaqa</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seru-epenisa-cakobau">Seru Epenisa Cakobau</a>, Bau dominated much of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a> through tribute and war. Cakobau's conversion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/methodism">Methodism</a> in 1854 and his victory at Kaba in 1855, with Tongan help, confirmed his power.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seru-epenisa-cakobau">Cakobau</a>, styling himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tui-viti">Tui Viti</a>, rivalled the Tongan chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enele-maafu">Maʻafu</a> and his <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tovata-confederacy">Tovata Confederacy</a>. In 1871 he became head of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-fiji">Kingdom of Fiji</a>, and in 1874 he ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-fiji">Colony of Fiji</a>. Bau remains the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kubuna-confederacy">Kubuna</a> confederacy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-bau.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Bau" width="320" height="204"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Nevers at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%8EleBau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1760 CE – 1871 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Naulivou, Tanoa Visawaqa, Seru Epenisa Cakobau</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Fijian traditional religion, later Methodism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Fijian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/fiji">Fiji</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bau, Kubuna Confederacy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1816&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bau" aria-label="Kingdom of Bau on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="9525 2844 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Bau lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M9845 3100L9855 3090"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M9855 3090h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9845 3100h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M9845 3100h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bau. <a href="/atlas?year=1816&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bau">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
